                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Dr. Gaurav Singh is Professor (Education) at the School of Education, IGNOU, and holding the responsibility of the National Co-cordinator of SWAYAMPRABHA-IGNOU Channels. He has previously worked as Professor (Educational Technology) at CIET, NCERT, New Delhi, and as Professor at the Central University of Haryana. At IGNOU, he coordinated the B.Ed. programme and served as the first Channel Coordinator of SWAYAMPRABHA Channel 32 (Teacher Education) and later Channel 20 (SOUs and Teacher Education). <br>
<br>
He holds an M.Sc. (Chemistry), M.Ed. (Gold Medal), PGDDE (Gold Medal), UGC-NET (Education), and a Ph.D. in Teacher Education. Since beginning his career in 2003, he has made significant contributions to teacher education, educational technology, and online learning. <br>
<br>
Dr. Singh has published 36 research papers, authored over 40 ODL course units, developed 125+ MOOC lectures, and coordinated nearly 1,200 lectures for SWAYAM and SWAYAMPRABHA. He has authored a book on Teacher Education and supervised Ph.D. scholars in E-learning and ICT. 
<br>
He has offered five MOOCs that have benefited nearly 80,000 learners. His course on Research Ethics and Plagiarism has been adopted by around 40 universities for Ph.D. coursework and ranks among the top-rated SWAYAM courses. <br>
<br>
Dr. Singh has received several prestigious recognitions, including the Commonwealth of Learning–AAOU Fellowship (2018), AAOU Silver Medal for Best Practices, the NIOS Distinguished Distance Educator Award, and the Best SWAYAM Course Award (2021). His research interests include Research Methodology, ICT in Education, Open and Distance Learning, and Teacher Education.</p>
