                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p align="justify">Dr. Ajith Kumar is serving as Associate Professor at the School of Education, IGNOU. His
academic journey is marked by notable achievements, beginning with his completion of M.Sc.
in Physics and then M.Ed. in Science Education from Mahatma Gandhi University, Kerala.</p>
<p align="justify">Later he completed M.Phil. in Education from the University of Calicut, Kerala and earned his
Ph.D. from IASE, Jamia Millia Islamia, New Delhi.</p>
<p align="justify">Commencing his career as a Higher Secondary Physics Teacher, Dr. Ajith later shifted to
teacher training, accumulating over 20 years of valuable teaching experience. His commitment
to education is evident through his extensive scholarly contributions, including the publication
of edited books and over 55 research papers and articles in national and international journals.
Additionally, he has written self-learning units/modules for various Open and Distance
Learning (ODL) institutions. He has also attended and presented research papers in various
seminars and conferences held across the country.</br>
<p align="justify">Dr. Ajith’s areas of academic interests are educational technology, statistics in research, science
education, teacher education, higher education, and open and distance learning. His expertise
has been shared through more than 350 invited talks, encompassing national and international
seminars, UGC-Human Resource Development Centres (HRDCs), and as a resource person in
workshops and teacher training programs nationwide. He has also developed over 70 video
lectures for SWAYAM-Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) and contributed video lectures
to Swayam Prabha channel. Moreover, he has developed eContent for various courses and
delivered more than 100 live lectures through Radio and Television (Gyandarshan). He is
actively engaged with national and international academic organizations such as CEMCA,
NCERT, NIOS, CBSE, UGC, NTA, etc.</p>
<p align="justify">Dr. Ajith currently serves as the coordinator for the Post Graduate Diploma in Educational
Technology (PGDET). Additionally, he oversees various courses within the School of
Education, IGNOU, and is presently supervising two doctoral research scholars. His
commitment extends globally, evidenced by his coordination of a staff development training
program, 'ICTs for Distance and Online Learning,' for higher education teachers in Guyana
(South America).</p>
<p align="justify">Dr. Ajith's leadership extends to his role as the coordinator of Channel 16 of Swayamprabha
and as the course coordinator of two MOOCs, namely 'ICT in Education' and 'Selection and
Integration of Technology in Educational Processes,' offered through SWAYAM. His
multifaceted contributions highlight his dedication to advancing education through innovative
methodologies and collaborative initiatives.</p></br>
